course: dictionary
lesson: 14811
title: Pursuant to: words in rules
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to official writing, such as school rules, council letters and legal papers. «Pursuant to the school rules, phones must be switched off in class.» Pursuant is a hard word, but the phrase pursuant to gives you a clue: the words after it name the rule that comes first.
explain: Try the swap check. Replace pursuant to with according to: «According to the school rules, phones must be switched off in class.» It still makes sense, so pursuant to means according to. The meaning is the same, only the style is more formal.
explain: When you see pursuant to, look for the rule, law or agreement it points to. The rest of the sentence then tells you what must happen because of that rule.
fact: Pursuant means following or according to a rule, law or agreement.
fact: Pursuant is usually used in the phrase «pursuant to».
fact: «Pursuant to the agreement» means according to the agreement.
fact: Formal writing uses words like pursuant so that rules sound official and exact.
fact: In everyday English, according to or following does the same job, so you can use those when you speak or write to friends.
exercise: «Pursuant to the library rules, books must be returned in two weeks.» What does pursuant to mean here? | *According to | Without any reason | Against | After lunch
exercise: Which everyday words mean the same as pursuant to? | Opposite | Under the table | Before | *According to
exercise: In «Pursuant to the law, parents must send children to school», what is the rule? | Children | *The law | Parents | School
test: «Pursuant to the rules, the game will start at noon.» Pursuant means | Far from the rules | *Following the rules | Very loud | Very fast
test: Mum writes, «Pursuant to our agreement, you may stay up late on Friday.» Which is a simple way to say pursuant to? | Far from our | Without our | Instead of our | *According to our
exam: Ms Ahmed writes, «Pursuant to the agreement, the trip is cancelled.» What does pursuant to mean? | Ignoring the agreement | Very angry about the agreement | *Following or according to the agreement | Happy to forget the agreement
